{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"bd141699cf8da9ee41e45b48c98d8ce5540704510081f4441907f507c67b75ad","digest":{"component_or_area":"Compaction sweep and triggering","key_entities":["compact-all","compact_cli","_scan_snapshot_state","compact.threshold","_compact_locked","_compact_policy","is_foldable",".github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml","transition_close","run_sweep","_spawn_detached_drain","stamped_file_is_stale","compact_trigger","_build_authorship_ledger","build_ticket_position_commit_map"],"problem_keywords":["compaction","event store","lock contention","out-of-band triggers","git history walk performance"],"propositions":["Compaction was removed from the close path to fix a 13m53s lock hold, but left stores with no standing automatic trigger, especially affecting CI-less deployments.","The scheduled sweep (6-hourly) works where CI exists, but stores without CI or cron need an operation-linked fallback that does not reintroduce the original P0 lock hold.","Sweep selection must reuse the fold's own foldable-event predicate and horizon to avoid re-selecting tickets whose excess events are all young, preventing permanent churn.","The sweep-scale history walk (one `git log --full-history` per ticket, inside the write lock) recreates bug 7084 at a larger scale, requiring the walk to be hoisted out of the lock and amortized across all tickets."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787525348477274001,"uuid":"0558ffd5-85fe-4462-9118-f3fbeccb33a1"}